# v0.25.5 — Audit reconciliation: register fully closed, fleet hardening, dead-code removal

**Baseline**: end of `v0.25.4` coverage at `a47ae3715` (2026-09-05).
**Date**: 2026-09-07.
**Tag**: `v0.25.5` (pending).

This release covers the 136 commits between the end of the `v0.25.4` change log
and `main` (`2b112f9f46`). The headline is the complete reconciliation of the
six-artifact open-items register: all 8 lanes (C, S, A, B, P, F, O, D) are now
at 0 items. 34 register items were closed across Tiers 0–7, the fleet was
deployed to `main` tip, and the last remaining flagged items from the fleet
audit were resolved or verified as non-issues.

## Register reconciliation

The six-artifact register (AITBC Static Audit · Escrow Settlement Triage · The
Open Arcs · The 1804 Freeze · Remediation Docket · TASKLIST.md) is now fully
closed. Every item was re-derived against current source and the five live
hosts before disposition. Items were closed with commit citations, struck as
stale, converted to operator decisions, or verified as already resolved.

### Lane 1 — Chain & consensus (C) · all closed

- **C-1** — Proposer hang at height 1804: root cause traced to a silent hung
  proposer task (no crash, no traceback). Watchdog added (`227bb9e105`) +
  per-phase debug tracing added (`87e11d7118`). The failure mode is converted
  from "silent" to "loud and located". Closed in Tier-6.
- **C-2** — Host-level outage: live fleet exercise executed (node1 stopped
  to simulate outage). Finding: chain stalled because
  `consensus_proposer_round_seconds` defaulted to 2× heartbeat interval.
  Fixed (`e8e9a91b04`): round timeout aligned to heartbeat (`max(30,
  max_empty_block_interval)` = 60s). `CONSENSUS_PROPOSER_ROUND_SECONDS=60`
  set on all 5 nodes. 5 regression tests. Closed in Tier-4 + Tier-5.
- **C-3** — Dead `enforce_state_root_validation` flag removed (`3e9a648bab`).
  The real gate is `sync_state_root_validation_enabled` (default True).
- **C-4** — `_process_txs_parallel` write-phase rollback added
  (`a7dd35c85a`). Session rollback on failure, matching other
  `_propose_block` failure exits. 3 tests.
- **C-5** — Closed in Tier-0 (bridge flags verified on all five hosts).
- **C-6** — Trap comment added at `config.py:600` (`8cff16db7a`).
- **C-7** — Closed in Tier-0 (bridge flags `true` on all five hosts).

### Lane 2 — Settlement & escrow (S) · all closed

- **S-1** — Closed in Tier-0.
- **S-2** — Escrow dedupe gaps closed (`53c1b6d608`): `_find_existing_lock`
  mirrors release/refund lookups; idempotency guard in `create_escrow` (409
  on param mismatch, 200 + settled state on true retry); double-lock refusal
  in `_create_token_escrow`. Sweeper lock added (`374988beeb`): `run_once`
  runs under `filelock`; losing worker skips. Gate coverage fixed (`53c1b6d608`):
  `escrowed_at IS NOT NULL` gate dropped; `status=='escrowed'` is sufficient.
- **S-3** — Auto-adjudication implemented (`f9aa1df824`):
  `POST /v1/admin/disputes/auto-adjudicate` scans DISPUTED payments for
  spot-check mismatch evidence; mismatches auto-refund + slash. 3 tests.
- **S-4** — Per-escrow addresses for escrow custody (`3ba7328768`): Option B
  implemented — each escrow gets a unique derived address, eliminating the
  shared-custody problem. ESCROW_LOCK credits `escrow:<job_id>`;
  RELEASE/REFUND debit it. v1/v2 backward compatible. 4 tests; 862 total
  blockchain-node tests green.
- **S-5** — Receipt drift mechanism fixed (`7a3e664eb6`): `execute_job` no
  longer adopts caller-supplied `result["receipt"]` when a signed `JobReceipt`
  exists. 3 regression tests. Historical residue formally written off by
  operator.
- **S-6** — Gate check verified: 0 of 48 refunded rows lack a hash on hub.
- **S-7** — Closed in Tier-0.
- **S-8** — Closed in Tier-3 (nginx `real_ip_recursive` fix deployed).

