## Fleet deployment

- All five hosts updated from `b0d5fc1a5` to `6ee9e5c74` (121 commits) on
  7 Sep. Sequence: node0 → node1 → hub2 → hub. Per-host: snapshot, git
  reset, update.sh, schema repair, daemon-reload, restart. All converged at
  height 4400, hash `0xbdc5e38b…`.
- hub2/node1 needed 3 alembic migrations; hub/node0 DBs already at head.
- Chain DBs needed `verify-db-schema.py --repair` for energy-quote columns.
- `aitbc-blockchain-{node,p2p,rpc}.service` gained
  `EnvironmentFile=-/etc/aitbc/validator-secrets.env`.
- `aitbc-island-ipfs.service` gained `After=/Wants=aitbc-coordinator-api.service`.
- `CONSENSUS_PROPOSER_ROUND_SECONDS=60` set on all 5 nodes.
- All five hosts have scoped validator secrets (`validator-secrets.env`).

## Known limitations & notes

- The exact await that hung the proposer at height 1804 is unprovable from
  logs alone (zero logging between heartbeat lines). The watchdog + per-phase
  tracing convert the failure mode from "silent" to "loud and located" — the
  next stall will show exactly which phase blocked.
- `gitea-local` tea login on `gitea-runner` is configured but the container
  has no `/opt/aitbc` checkout — tea commands that require a repo context
  will fail. The login itself is valid.
- The six-artifact register is now fully closed. No open items remain.

## 2026-09-08 post-audit corrections

A read-only Gitea Actions API audit (`tea api` on `hub.aitbc`) and live host
inspection updated the following conclusions:

- **D-2 — Mesh gossip auth gap** is closed on `main` at `252469f3b` (same tree
  as the cited branch commit `761b887837`) plus the two fixes `b990194ed7` and
  `20257c5975`. The `origin/feat/open-island-gossip-remediation` branch still
  carries four unmerged commits unrelated to the auth gap.
- **O-3 — `redis.env`** exists only on `hub.aitbc` and `node2`; no systemd unit
  on any host loads it. The actual Redis credentials live in
  `/etc/aitbc/blockchain-secrets.env` and `redis.conf`. Status narrowed, not
  fully closed.
- **CI history** — Gitea Actions runs 19600–19638 were consecutive failures
  (39 runs, not the 22 noted earlier). 19639 (`b62637a792`) is the first green
  gate in that window; 19642 (`3d09e81054`) also failed, with the green follow-up
  at 19643 (`c79462f3e`). 19644–19646 are green.
- **Fleet at 8 Sep 10:xx** is at `origin/main` tip `8cb48178d5`. All five
  `aitbc-blockchain-node/rpc` services are active and `/health` returns `ok`;
  `hub`, `hub2`, `node1`, and `node2` are at block 5130, while `node0` is at
  5128 (two blocks behind at the time of inspection).
